{
  "case_id": "2017-17-2",
  "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: It actually requires a search. It's -- the disclosure here is really a substitute for the government's searching. The Act permits the government to have a warrant and go in and search for these materials or, in the alternative, to ask the source to do its own search and then turn the materials over."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Department of Justice",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: So, Justice Sotomayor, it -- it's a hybrid instrument that has two functions. The first function operates directly on the provider. It requires a provider to make disclosure of information. That is a function that's classically performed by a subpoena or a discovery order."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: In that sense, is it -- is it correct to say that the parties agree that the Act does not have extraterritorial application?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Department of Justice",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: We read it against the backdrop of this Court's decision in Morrison and RJR, which provide that unless the statute clearly has extraterritorial application in its text, structure, or operation, it has none."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. Dreeben, why would that be the case using the focus test that we wouldn't take cognizance of the fact that the information must be collected abroad and transmitted from abroad to the United States before it could then be disclosed? I mean, there's a chain of activity that's required here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Could I ask you one\nother question? What is happening when these\norders are sought now outside of the Second\nCircuit? I mean, there's been talk about\nleaving things alone, but is the rest of the\ncountry going -- are the judges everywhere in\nthe country going to follow what the Second\nCircuit decided? Are they doing that, or are\nthey continuing to issue the kinds of orders\nthat were issued in the past?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I see the problem, I\nthink, but what I don't see yet -- maybe I just\nhave to go back and study it -- is -- is your\nanswer to Justice Gorsuch's question, which has\nbeen bothering me on both sides. They're with\nyou on this, you know, but I look at the\nlanguage of the statute, and the statute says:\nA government entity \"may require the disclosure\nby a provider of electronic communication ...\nonly pursuant to a warrant issued using the\nprocedures described in the Federal Rules of\nCriminal Procedure.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But you are agreeing,\nMr. Dreeben, that a court in that circumstance\nshould conduct a comity analysis?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Microsoft",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROSENKRANZ: Mr. Chief Justice,\nand may it please the Court:\nI'll start where Justice Kennedy\nstarted, which is where we all agree that the\nStored Communications Act is limited to the\nUnited States. Yet the government wants to use\nthe act to unilaterally reach into a foreign\nland to search for, copy, and import private\ncustomer correspondence physically stored in a\ndigital lockbox in a foreign computer where\nit's protected by foreign law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Something has to happen electronically or with human intervention?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Microsoft",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A human being doesn't have to do it. It is a robot. And if you -\u00ad if you sent a robot into a foreign land to seize evidence, it would certainly implicate foreign interests."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you dispute that the government could issue a warrant to go ahead and do exactly that in Redmond?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Microsoft",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It would be an extraterritorial search; it would, therefore, be illegal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Microsoft",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's a basic physical property at issue here that underscores that this is not just some random act of putting e-mails in one place or another. There's this physical phenomenon called latency."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, if this person is not Irish and Ireland played no part in your decision to store the information there and there's nothing that Ireland could do about it if you chose tomorrow to move it someplace else, it is a little difficult for me to see what Ireland's interest is in this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Microsoft",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0002-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I disagree with the premise. This -- these e-mails have a physical presence. They are actually on a hard drive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
      "evidence_id": "ev-85e8c0d9c13f-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And it's not because Redmond, Washington, is not in New York. It's because warrants, although there is nationwide ability to reach evidence within the United States, warrants are not extraterritorial."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-17-2",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "85e8c0d9c13f4253b5926203aeae80277a3899c451e8600da80cac1a73d3b1d2",
